<% faqs = [
  [ "What is Flockwork?", "Flockwork is project planning software for churches. It keeps a project’s sign-ups, tasks, schedule and budget in one place, so meal trains, Vacation Bible School, workdays and retreats are easier to plan and simpler to fill." ],
  [ "How do volunteers sign up?", "You send one link in a text or the bulletin. People open it on any phone, see which spots are still open, and sign in with their email to take one." ],
  [ "Does Flockwork work with Planning Center?", "Yes. Your people come in from Planning Center or a CSV, so nobody types a roster twice. Registration and check-in on the day stay where they already are." ],
  [ "What does the Planner do?", "Tell it what you’re organizing in one sentence. It asks a few focused questions and suggests sign-ups, tasks, a schedule and a budget that you keep or drop. It plans from the project details and never sees your people directory." ],
  [ "Can I try it before setting up my church?", "Yes. The demo opens Flockwork with a sample church already full of projects and people, so you can click around before you add your own." ]
] %>
<% marketing_head(@page, type: "SoftwareApplication", faqs: faqs, node: { applicationCategory: "BusinessApplication", operatingSystem: "Web" }) %>
<section class="lp-hero" aria-labelledby="landing-title">
  <div class="header-wash" aria-hidden="true" data-controller="wash">
    <svg><filter id="wash-grain"><feTurbulence type="fractalNoise" baseFrequency=".85" numOctaves="2" stitchTiles="stitch"/><feColorMatrix values="0 0 0 0 .08 0 0 0 0 .08 0 0 0 0 .07 0 0 0 .1 0"/></filter><rect width="100%" height="100%" filter="url(#wash-grain)"/></svg>
  </div>
  <div class="lp-hero-copy">
    <h1 id="landing-title">Project planning for your church.</h1>
    <p>Meal trains, VBS, workdays, retreats: all the ways a church looks after its own. Flockwork makes them easier to plan and simpler to fill, so you can say yes to more of them.</p>
    <div class="lp-actions">
      <%= link_to "Plan Your First Project", sign_up_path, class: "btn btn-primary" %>
      <%= link_to "See the Demo", new_demo_session_path, class: "btn btn-secondary" %>
    </div>
  </div>
  <%= render "landing/scene", name: "hero", width: 1110, height: 640, class: "lp-hero-scene lp-float", loading: "eager", fetchpriority: "high",
        alt: "Daniel’s Home lists Grace Fellowship’s active projects: a meal train, Vacation Bible School, a church workday and a women’s retreat. On her phone, Ruth signs up to bring dinner for the meal train, and its row on Home goes from 15 to 14 dinners still needing someone" %>
</section>

<%= render "landing/photos" %>

<%= render "landing/between" %>

<%= render "landing/planner" %>

<%= render "landing/tour" %>

<section class="lp-section" aria-labelledby="people-title">
  <div class="lp-intro">
    <h2 id="people-title">Made for the people who show up.</h2>
    <p>Flockwork keeps track of the work, so leaders have more time for the people doing it.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="lp-bento">
    <article class="lp-card lp-card-tall">
      <div class="lp-card-copy"><h3>One link, from any phone</h3><p>Send it in a text or a bulletin. People see what’s still open and take the day that works for them.</p></div>
      <%= render "landing/scene", name: "card-signup", width: 456, height: 720, class: "lp-scene", alt: "The public sign-up page for the Alvarez family meal train on a phone, where someone picks a dinner that had one spot left" %>
    </article>
    <article class="lp-card">
      <div class="lp-card-copy"><h3>Know your people</h3><p>See who’s serving, who’s away and who hasn’t been asked yet. Bring them in from Planning Center or a CSV.</p></div>
      <%= render "landing/scene", name: "card-people", width: 640, height: 280, class: "lp-scene", alt: "The People directory switching from Everyone to Not yet asked, which lists the people no one has invited yet" %>
    </article>
    <article class="lp-card">
      <div class="lp-card-copy"><h3>Notice who’s carrying too much</h3><p>See who’s on too many projects before they burn out. Plain counts, never scores, and a check-in is one tap.</p></div>
      <%= render "landing/scene", name: "card-oversight", width: 640, height: 280, class: "lp-scene", alt: "Maria Lopez serves on four active projects with no check-in logged. A check-in is logged, and the card reads Checked in today by Daniel Okafor" %>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<%= render "landing/why" %>

<section class="lp-section lp-faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="lp-intro">
    <h2 id="faq-title">Questions, answered.</h2>
    <p>The short version of what churches ask before their first project.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="lp-faq-list">
    <% faqs.each do |question, answer| %>
      <div class="lp-faq-item"><h3><%= question %></h3><p><%= answer %></p></div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="lp-close" aria-labelledby="close-title">
  <h2 id="close-title">Say yes to the next one.</h2>
  <p>Start with one project. Invite the people who make it happen.</p>
  <%= link_to "Plan Your First Project", sign_up_path, class: "btn btn-primary" %>
  <p class="lp-returning">Already part of a church here? <%= link_to "Sign in", new_sign_in_request_path, class: "link font-medium" %></p>
</section>
